/E (Leeks trap dirt between their layers, so prep matters as much as cooking. Cut off the dark green tops and the root end, slice the white and pale green part lengthwise, then rinse really well between the layers. After that, slice it into thin half-moons. Let the leek soften slowly in olive oil and salt until she loses her edges and turns silky. Around 6-8 minutes on medium-low heat. No browning. )
